From a9ea9c284d110649bd8c6426151c08cbce4f021f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:29:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Camera play: one more player can join those who play
 already

camera_play.join lets a person play with the camera among people whose
moves are planned already (someone taking over a place in the audience):
plan_camera_play takes those people and their moves as `planned`, puts
them into the room first (where they travel, where their elbows, hands and
head go) and plans the new moves clear of them as of everyone else; the
others' plays stay as they are. The person's behaviour is wrapped in a
CameraPlay and gets a PlayPose, with the same exceptions as play_along.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B99J6LuDFd7VnzjjcAYtWv
