The book's look at the created/ folder is quick now: a character's images
are read from their files the first time they are used (Textures, safe
from several threads), so the demo decodes them on the thread that makes
the character's 3D person instead of stalling the video (about 30 ms per
1024x1024 image). A missing image is still found when the character is
loaded. apply_looks takes off what a person wore before, takes item looks
from a wardrobe and finds item image files in the character's own folder.

