From ba58d8cbe3aeb7dc9706bb00ce9bf22bac3c4fb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Created characters in the fair: they take over places,
 live

scenes/created_cast.py puts the characters of the created/ folder into the
fair, each in the place of one of the fair's own grown-ups who walk about:
the visitors who walk up to the camera first, then walkers, then wanderers;
never a child's place. A place whose person is like the avatar (same sex
and age group, so the same clips and stride) comes first within each kind:
the new 3D person gets the place's behaviour and camera play as they are,
the swap is exact. Elsewhere the behaviour is made again for the avatar
(crowd.Recipe: same path, pauses and seed; its own clips, walking as fast
as the person before when its clips keep up within 25 %, so the feet never
slide), fitted in among everyone (fair.fit_in: keep_apart's 0.6 m for one
newcomer, following the old timing as closely as it can) and given camera
play around the others' (fair.join_camera_play); it is swapped in when it
stands where the person it replaces stands. The 3D person keeps the place's
name, and person.created marks it: the known faces of recognition.cast
leave it alone, selection mode tags it with the character's name, and it
wears the character's textures and items.

The demo owns a CharacterBook of created/ (--created DIR, DemoConfig.created)
and keeps the scene in step once a second: a new character joins the next
free place ("Ada joined the fair", and a status line), a changed one is
updated in place, a deleted one gives the place back; restarting and
reloading the scene keep them. Making the 3D people (0.05-0.6 s) runs on a
worker thread; the main thread spends under 2 ms on it per frame. README
section "Created characters", docs/previews/created_characters.jpg.

