From f88536be0d66f2b4d224b365e8cfc8314eb6ee42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:53:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Created characters in the fair: unseen swaps, a paced
 worker, bad looks reported

Fixes from the review of the step:

- A newcomer with a behaviour of its own is swapped in only when nobody sees
  it happen (swap_cost): where the person it replaces stands, or neither of
  them in the camera's picture. Before, a hidden occupant was enough, and a
  child with a longer loop could appear mid-aisle. Without such a moment for
  LINE_UP seconds, a jump of up to POP (2 m) or a pop in view is allowed;
  after twice that, anything. On the real fair no swap waits that long.
- The worker thread is paced (new bifold_demo.pacing). Long computations
  call pause() between steps, and a paced thread rests three quarters of the
  time, so it no longer holds the GIL against the main thread. Measured at
  30 fps on the real fair with three characters joining: frames take 13-18 ms
  (median) while one is being made, against 30 ms unpaced, and up to 3 in a
  hundred are late, against almost half. Behaviour.positions is vectorised
  per piece.
- Bad looks no longer crash the demo. A changed character's textures are
  made on the worker. A failure in the main-thread apply_looks leaves the
  character as it was and is reported. apply_looks leaves out items it
  cannot wear and returns why. load() and save() refuse item looks of the
  wrong kind.
- A place freed by a character that cannot be made goes to one that waits.
- Characters joining together get one notice ("Ada and Ben joined the fair").
- stand_in reports when fit_in cannot keep 0.6 m. join_camera_play looks at
  the others as planned (fair.planned_behaviour), not at selection mode's
  live Performer.
- The docs say how closely rebuilt places follow the old timing (roughly; in
  some places metres apart for long stretches). A real-avatar test covers
  every visitor's place rebuilt.

