From 2d0a1c37687a890910df7bc8d1ae270c27320203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:57:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Created characters in the fair: changes nobody sees, a
 book that never stops the demo

Every change of a place (a character coming in, another avatar, new looks,
a character leaving) is now made only at a frame where nothing of it shows.
The renderer counts the pixels the person leaving and the one coming in
would have in the frame just drawn (Renderer.visible_pixels: occlusion
queries, depth only). The one there is taken out at such a frame, the place
stays empty until the newcomer would show no pixel either, and then they are
there. After 20 s of scene time without such a moment, a frame where the
change shows at most 0.05 % of the picture will do (someone far down the
hall, or nearly hidden), never more. This replaces the coincidence rule,
which swapped in plain view, turned people round and, after a minute, let
them jump or pop. Leaving goes the same way, and a freed place goes to a
character waiting for one without its own person in between. Restarting
(R) and reloading the scene make the changes at once. A sign is held up
from the start (it no longer drops to the hip a second after joining).

What drawing a newcomer needs goes to the GPU over the frames before they
come in: Renderer.prepare uploads one texture (or its mipmaps) a frame, and
textures made on the worker are laid out for the upload there
(textures.prepare_upload).

The book (characters/created.py) never raises for what is in the folder:
a character.json of any shape is a problem of the book (load() checks every
field), the folder itself vanishing or not listable leaves the characters as
they are, and a character that could be read before stays as it was while
its file does not read well (an editor or a copy writing it in place).
Problems are told when they turn up and again when they come back. Any file
of a character's folder changing is a change, so a half-copied image is read
again once whole; a file written again unchanged is no change. Images of any
PNG kind are read (16 bits, grey, a palette) and scaled down to 1024 pixels.
Item pictures are files of the character's folder only, read on the worker,
and kept when the character is saved again. Saving a name whose folder holds
another character ("Ada?" over "Ada") is refused, a copied folder is
reported, and so are textures for parts the avatar does not have.

The worker: jobs someone waits for (the start, a scene reload) hurry instead
of resting (0.5 s for four characters, 1.4 s for thirteen; it was 3.6 to
3.8 and 7.0 to 7.8 s), close() stops a job at its next pause (quitting no longer waits),
characters in a place like their avatar are paced too, newcomers made at the
same time are planned around each other (0.6 m), one that could not be made
is tried again every 10 s, and one deleted while it is made is no error.
DemoApp merges the created characters' notices while one is on the screen,
and a full fair says who waits instead of "no place". behaviour._plan finds
its start in O(n log m) (a 53 ms stretch without a pause), and
_WalkPiece.floor no longer claims the same numbers to the last bit.

Tests: the unseen-change rule (synthetic views and rendered real avatars),
book files of 30 wrong shapes, folder races, retries, the sign, notices,
hurry and cancel, newcomers keeping apart, join planned around the players
(mutant: planned=[] now fails) and the yoga rank (now tested). README and
docs/previews/created_swaps.jpg: how changes are made where nobody sees
them, with frame times measured in the demo's own loop.

